  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/MrMints/shinydex/zipball/v1.0.0",
  "body": "## Native Windows desktop app\nDownload **ShinyDex.exe** below and run it to install ShinyDex. Open the desktop shortcut or Start menu entry. Windows 10/11 x64; no separately installed Node.js or Python is required.\n\n- Opens its own desktop window with all artwork included. No browser launcher, localhost server, or port 5173 is required.\n- New desktop releases offer **Update now** and **Later** at startup. The version dropdown supports installing another published desktop version, including rollback. This is the first desktop release, so versions below 1.0.0 and historical browser previews are excluded.\n- Downloads use immutable release feeds and are verified using the manifest SHA-512 and GitHub SHA-256 digest before automatic installation and restart. The installed app remains usable if checks or downloads fail.\n- Collection files live in `%APPDATA%\\ShinyDexDesktop` across future desktop updates and rollbacks, with a local backup before installation. IDs from newer catalogs are preserved by older desktop versions. Collections are never uploaded to GitHub.\n- This release starts a fresh desktop profile. Automatic migration from browser preview saves is not included. Export and import compatible version-2 JSON backups from the app.\n\nThe installer is unsigned; Windows may show a publisher/SmartScreen prompt. Verify it with **ShinyDex.exe.sha256**. **latest.yml** and the blockmap support future in-app updates.\n\nValidation: all 33 existing project checks and 5 desktop regression tests passed. Source, packaged, and installed desktop smoke tests verified rendering, reload persistence, renderer isolation, and updater controls. The packaged app worked with port 5173 occupied; the native main process opened no TCP listener during testing. NSIS installation and test uninstallation succeeded. Update/downgrade calls were checked with controlled fixtures; installation from a future public desktop release and clean-machine Windows prompts remain unverified.\n\nThe comprehensive hunting, historical event, transfer-prerequisite, and attribution audits remain incomplete. This release does not certify exhaustive game data.\n"
